import Mathlib
import InverseGalois.Solvable.SemiabelianCriterion
import InverseGalois.Solvable.SemiabelianSmall

/-!
# Groups of order `p ^ 4` are semiabelian

The covering criterion of `InverseGalois.Solvable.SemiabelianCriterion` turns an abelian normal
subgroup of prime index into membership in Dentzer's class of semiabelian groups, and
`InverseGalois.Solvable.SemiabelianSmall` feeds it with Sylow subgroups to cover the orders `p`,
`p ^ 2`, `p ^ 3` and `p * q`.  The next prime power, `p ^ 4`, is out of reach of Sylow's theorem
alone: a subgroup of order `p ^ 3` in a group of order `p ^ 4` need not be abelian.  What replaces
it is a classical counting argument of Burnside, which produces an abelian normal subgroup of
index at most `p` in any group of order `p ^ 4`.

The argument revolves around a subgroup `A` that is *maximal* among the abelian normal subgroups
of a finite `p`-group `G`; such a subgroup exists because the trivial subgroup is abelian and
normal and there are only finitely many subgroups.  The key structural fact is that a maximal
abelian normal subgroup is *self-centralizing*: `A` certainly lies inside its own centralizer `C`,
and `C` is normal because `A` is, so if the inclusion were strict then the nontrivial normal
subgroup `C ⧸ A` of the `p`-group `G ⧸ A` would meet the centre of `G ⧸ A`.  An element `x` of `C`
whose class is central and nontrivial then enlarges `A` to `A ⊔ ⟨x⟩`, which is still normal — its
image in `G ⧸ A` is central — and still abelian — `x` centralizes `A` — contradicting maximality.
The fact that a nontrivial normal subgroup of a finite `p`-group meets the centre is itself the
orbit-counting congruence for the conjugation action of `G` on that subgroup.

Self-centralizing pins down the size of `A` when `G` has order `p ^ 4`.  Orders `1` and `p` are
impossible: a normal subgroup of order dividing `p` is generated by a central element, so its
centralizer is all of `G`, forcing `A = G`.  Order `p ^ 2` is impossible as well, and this is the
heart of the matter.  Write `B` for the intersection of `A` with the centre of `G`; it is
nontrivial by the centre-meeting principle and proper in `A` because `A` is not central, so it has
order exactly `p`.  Choosing `x` in `A` whose class generates a central subgroup of `G ⧸ B` makes
the commutator map `g ↦ g x g⁻¹ x⁻¹` a homomorphism from `G` to `B`, since all its values are
central.  Its kernel consists of the elements commuting with `x`, hence with `B ⊔ ⟨x⟩ = A`, hence
lies in the centralizer of `A`, which is `A`; so the index `p ^ 2` of `A` is bounded by the order
`p` of `B`, which is absurd.  Only the orders `p ^ 3` and `p ^ 4` remain, i.e. `A` has index `p`
or `1`, and the criterion of the previous files applies.

## Main results

* `Semiabelian.exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot` — a nontrivial normal subgroup of a finite `p`-group
  contains a nontrivial element of the centre of the whole group.
* `Semiabelian.exists_maximal_abelian_normal` — a finite group has an abelian normal subgroup that
  is maximal among the abelian normal subgroups.
* `Semiabelian.centralizer_eq_of_maximal_abelian_normal` — **a maximal abelian normal subgroup of
  a finite `p`-group is its own centralizer**.
* `Semiabelian.card_ne_prime_sq_of_centralizer_eq` — in a group of order `p ^ 4`, a
  self-centralizing abelian normal subgroup does not have order `p ^ 2`.
* `Semiabelian.exists_abelian_normal_index_le` — **a group of order `p ^ 4` has an abelian normal
  subgroup of index `1` or `p`**.
* `IsSemiabelian.of_card_eq_prime_pow_four` — **every group of order `p ^ 4` is semiabelian**.
-/

namespace Semiabelian

/-- **A nontrivial normal subgroup `N` of a finite `p`-group `G` meets the centre of `G`.**  The
group `G` acts on `N` by conjugation, an action available because `N` is normal, and the number of
fixed points of a `p`-group acting on a finite set is congruent to the size of the set modulo `p`.
Here the size of `N` is a positive power of `p` and the identity is a fixed point, so the fixed
points — the elements of `N` that commute with everything in `G` — number at least `p`, leaving
room for one other than the identity. -/
theorem exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)
    (hG : IsPGroup p G) (N : Subgroup G) [N.Normal] (hN : N ≠ ⊥) :
    ∃ x ∈ N, x ∈ Subgroup.center G ∧ x ≠ 1 := by
  haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨hp⟩
  have hNnt : Nontrivial ↥N := N.nontrivial_iff_ne_bot.mpr hN
  have hNp : IsPGroup p ↥N := hG.to_subgroup N
  have hdvd : p ∣ Nat.card ↥N := by
    obtain ⟨n, hn0, hn⟩ := hNp.nontrivial_iff_card.mp hNnt
    exact hn ▸ dvd_pow_self p hn0.ne'
  have hCA : IsPGroup p (ConjAct G) := hG.of_equiv ConjAct.toConjAct
  have h1 : (1 : ↥N) ∈ MulAction.fixedPoints (ConjAct G) ↥N := fun g => smul_one g
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hne⟩ := hCA.exists_fixed_point_of_prime_dvd_card_of_fixed_point (α := ↥N) hdvd h1
  refine ⟨(b : G), b.2, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Subgroup.mem_center_iff]
    intro g
    have hfix := hb (ConjAct.toConjAct g)
    have h2 : (ConjAct.toConjAct g) • (b : G) = (b : G) := congrArg Subtype.val hfix
    rw [ConjAct.toConjAct_smul] at h2
    calc g * (b : G) = g * (b : G) * g⁻¹ * g := by group
      _ = (b : G) * g := by rw [h2]
  · intro h
    exact hne (Subtype.ext h.symm)

/-- **A finite group has a maximal abelian normal subgroup.**  The abelian normal subgroups form a
nonempty family — the trivial subgroup belongs to it — inside the finite partial order of all
subgroups, and a nonempty family in a finite partial order has a maximal member. -/
theorem exists_maximal_abelian_normal {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] :
    ∃ A : Subgroup G, A.Normal ∧ (∀ u v : ↥A, u * v = v * u) ∧
      ∀ B : Subgroup G, B.Normal → (∀ u v : ↥B, u * v = v * u) → A ≤ B → B = A := by
  obtain ⟨A, -, hAmax⟩ := Finite.exists_le_maximal (a := (⊥ : Subgroup G))
    (p := fun B : Subgroup G => B.Normal ∧ ∀ u v : ↥B, u * v = v * u)
    ⟨inferInstance, fun u v => by rw [Subsingleton.elim u 1, one_mul, mul_one]⟩
  exact ⟨A, hAmax.1.1, hAmax.1.2, fun B hB hBc hAB => le_antisymm (hAmax.2 ⟨hB, hBc⟩ hAB) hAB⟩

/-- **A maximal abelian normal subgroup of a finite `p`-group is its own centralizer.**  The
inclusion of `A` in its centralizer `C` is the commutativity of `A`, and `C` is normal because `A`
is.  Were the inclusion strict, the image of `C` in `G ⧸ A` would be a nontrivial normal subgroup
of a finite `p`-group and so would contain a nontrivial central element, say the class of some
`x ∈ C \ A`.  Adjoining `x` to `A` produces a subgroup that is normal, because conjugates of `x`
differ from `x` by elements of `A`, and abelian, because `x` centralizes `A` and powers of `x`
commute with one another.  That contradicts the maximality of `A`. -/
theorem centralizer_eq_of_maximal_abelian_normal {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] {p : ℕ}
    (hp : p.Prime) (hG : IsPGroup p G) (A : Subgroup G) [A.Normal]
    (hab : ∀ u v : ↥A, u * v = v * u)
    (hmax : ∀ B : Subgroup G, B.Normal → (∀ u v : ↥B, u * v = v * u) → A ≤ B → B = A) :
    Subgroup.centralizer (A : Set G) = A := by
  haveI : IsMulCommutative A := ⟨⟨hab⟩⟩
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Subgroup.le_centralizer A)
  by_contra hle
  set C : Subgroup G := Subgroup.centralizer (A : Set G)
  have hCbar : C.map (QuotientGroup.mk' A) ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    refine hle fun c hc => ?_
    have hc1 : (QuotientGroup.mk' A) c = 1 := by
      have hmem : (QuotientGroup.mk' A) c ∈ C.map (QuotientGroup.mk' A) := ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩
      rw [h] at hmem
      simpa using hmem
    simpa using (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff c).mp hc1
  haveI : (C.map (QuotientGroup.mk' A)).Normal :=
    Subgroup.Normal.map inferInstance _ (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective A)
  obtain ⟨y, hyC, hycen, hy1⟩ :=
    exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot hp (hG.to_quotient A) (C.map (QuotientGroup.mk' A)) hCbar
  obtain ⟨x, hxC, rfl⟩ := hyC
  have hxA : x ∉ A := by
    intro hx
    exact hy1 (by simpa using (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff x).mpr hx)
  have hxc : ∀ g : G, g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ A := by
    intro g
    have hcen := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp hycen ((QuotientGroup.mk' A) g)
    rw [← QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
    have hexp : ((g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ : G) : G ⧸ A) =
        (QuotientGroup.mk' A) g * (QuotientGroup.mk' A) x * ((QuotientGroup.mk' A) g)⁻¹ *
          ((QuotientGroup.mk' A) x)⁻¹ := by simp
    rw [hexp, hcen]
    group
  set B : Subgroup G := A ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x with hB
  have hxB : x ∈ B := Subgroup.mem_sup_right (Subgroup.mem_zpowers x)
  have hconj : ∀ g : G, g * x * g⁻¹ ∈ B := by
    intro g
    have hrw : g * x * g⁻¹ = (g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * x := by group
    rw [hrw]
    exact mul_mem (Subgroup.mem_sup_left (hxc g)) hxB
  have hBnormal : B.Normal := by
    constructor
    intro n hn g
    have hmaple : B.map (MulAut.conj g).toMonoidHom ≤ B := by
      rw [hB, Subgroup.map_sup, MonoidHom.map_zpowers]
      refine sup_le (fun z hz => ?_) (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr (hconj g))
      obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact Subgroup.mem_sup_left (‹A.Normal›.conj_mem a ha g)
    exact hmaple ⟨n, hn, rfl⟩
  have hBcomm : ∀ u v : ↥B, u * v = v * u := by
    have hBle : B ≤ Subgroup.centralizer (B : Set G) := by
      have hBA : B ≤ Subgroup.centralizer (A : Set G) :=
        sup_le (Subgroup.le_centralizer A) (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hxC)
      have hBx : B ≤ Subgroup.centralizer ((Subgroup.zpowers x : Subgroup G) : Set G) :=
        sup_le (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff.mpr (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hxC))
          (Subgroup.le_centralizer _)
      exact sup_le (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff.mpr hBA) (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff.mpr hBx)
    exact fun u v => (Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff_isMulCommutative.mp hBle).1.1 u v
  exact hxA (hmax B hBnormal hBcomm le_sup_left ▸ hxB)

/-- **In a group of order `p ^ 4`, a self-centralizing abelian normal subgroup does not have order
`p ^ 2`.**  Suppose it did, and let `B` be its intersection with the centre of `G`.  The
centre-meeting principle makes `B` nontrivial, while `B` is proper in `A` because a central `A`
would be its own centralizer only if it were the whole group; hence `B` has order `p`.  The
quotient `A ⧸ B` is nontrivial, so it contains an element whose class in `G ⧸ B` is central and
nontrivial; lift it to `x ∈ A`.  All commutators `g x g⁻¹ x⁻¹` then lie in `B` and so are central,
which makes `g ↦ g x g⁻¹ x⁻¹` a homomorphism `G → B`.  Its kernel is the set of elements commuting
with `x`; such an element also commutes with the central subgroup `B`, hence with the subgroup
generated by `B` and `x`, which is `A` for reasons of order, hence lies in the centralizer of `A`,
namely `A` itself.  The kernel is therefore exactly `A`, so the index `p ^ 2` of `A` is at most
the order `p` of `B`. -/
theorem card_ne_prime_sq_of_centralizer_eq {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)
    (hcard : Nat.card G = p ^ 4) (A : Subgroup G) [A.Normal] (hab : ∀ u v : ↥A, u * v = v * u)
    (hcent : Subgroup.centralizer (A : Set G) = A) : Nat.card ↥A ≠ p ^ 2 := by
  haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨hp⟩
  intro hA2
  have hG : IsPGroup p G := IsPGroup.of_card hcard
  set B : Subgroup G := A ⊓ Subgroup.center G
  have hBA : B ≤ A := inf_le_left
  have hBcen : B ≤ Subgroup.center G := inf_le_right
  haveI hBnormal : B.Normal := by
    constructor
    intro n hn g
    have hg := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (hBcen hn) g
    have hfix : g * n * g⁻¹ = n := by rw [hg]; group
    rw [hfix]
    exact hn
  have hAbot : A ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    rw [h, Subgroup.card_bot] at hA2
    exact (Nat.one_lt_pow two_ne_zero hp.one_lt).ne hA2
  obtain ⟨z, hzA, hzcen, hz1⟩ := exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot hp hG A hAbot
  have hBbot : B ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    have hzB : z ∈ B := Subgroup.mem_inf.mpr ⟨hzA, hzcen⟩
    rw [h] at hzB
    exact hz1 (by simpa using hzB)
  have hAcen : ¬ (A : Set G) ⊆ (Subgroup.center G : Set G) := by
    intro hsub
    have htop : A = ⊤ := by
      rw [← hcent, Subgroup.centralizer_eq_top_iff_subset]
      exact hsub
    rw [htop, Subgroup.card_top, hcard] at hA2
    exact absurd hA2.symm (Nat.pow_lt_pow_right hp.one_lt (by norm_num)).ne
  have hBne : B ≠ A := by
    intro h
    exact hAcen fun a ha => (h ▸ ha : a ∈ B).2
  have hBcard : Nat.card ↥B = p := by
    obtain ⟨k, hk, hkB⟩ := (Nat.dvd_prime_pow hp).mp (hA2 ▸ Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le hBA)
    interval_cases k
    · exact absurd (Subgroup.card_eq_one.mp (by simpa using hkB)) hBbot
    · simpa using hkB
    · exact absurd (Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hBA (by rw [hA2, hkB])) hBne
  have hABbot : A.map (QuotientGroup.mk' B) ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    refine hBne (le_antisymm hBA fun a ha => ?_)
    have hmem : (QuotientGroup.mk' B) a ∈ A.map (QuotientGroup.mk' B) := ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    rw [h] at hmem
    simpa using (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff a).mp (by simpa using hmem)
  haveI : (A.map (QuotientGroup.mk' B)).Normal :=
    Subgroup.Normal.map inferInstance _ (QuotientGroup.mk'_surjective B)
  obtain ⟨y, hyA, hycen, hy1⟩ :=
    exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot hp (hG.to_quotient B) (A.map (QuotientGroup.mk' B)) hABbot
  obtain ⟨x, hxA, rfl⟩ := hyA
  have hxB : x ∉ B := fun hx => hy1 (by simpa using (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff x).mpr hx)
  have hxc : ∀ g : G, g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ ∈ B := by
    intro g
    have hcen := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp hycen ((QuotientGroup.mk' B) g)
    rw [← QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
    have hexp : ((g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ : G) : G ⧸ B) =
        (QuotientGroup.mk' B) g * (QuotientGroup.mk' B) x * ((QuotientGroup.mk' B) g)⁻¹ *
          ((QuotientGroup.mk' B) x)⁻¹ := by simp
    rw [hexp, hcen]
    group
  have hDA : B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x ≤ A := sup_le hBA (Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hxA)
  have hDcard : Nat.card ↥(B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x) = p ^ 2 := by
    obtain ⟨k, hk, hkD⟩ := (Nat.dvd_prime_pow hp).mp (hA2 ▸ Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le hDA)
    have hBD : B ≤ B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x := le_sup_left
    have hne : B ≠ B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x := fun h =>
      hxB (h ▸ Subgroup.mem_sup_right (Subgroup.mem_zpowers x))
    have hlt : Nat.card ↥B < Nat.card ↥(B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x) := by
      refine lt_of_le_of_ne (Nat.le_of_dvd Nat.card_pos (Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le hBD)) ?_
      intro h
      exact hne (Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hBD h.ge)
    have hp2 := hp.two_le
    interval_cases k
    · simp only [pow_zero] at hkD
      omega
    · rw [pow_one] at hkD
      omega
    · exact hkD
  have hDeq : B ⊔ Subgroup.zpowers x = A := Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hDA (by rw [hA2, hDcard])
  have hkey : ∀ g h : G, (g * h) * x * (g * h)⁻¹ * x⁻¹ =
      (g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * (h * x * h⁻¹ * x⁻¹) := by
    intro g h
    have hcz := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (hBcen (hxc h))
    have hdz := Subgroup.mem_center_iff.mp (hBcen (hxc g))
    calc (g * h) * x * (g * h)⁻¹ * x⁻¹
        = (g * (h * x * h⁻¹ * x⁻¹)) * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ := by group
      _ = ((h * x * h⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * g) * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ := by rw [hcz g]
      _ = (h * x * h⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * (g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹) := by group
      _ = (g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹) * (h * x * h⁻¹ * x⁻¹) := by rw [hdz]
  set φ : G →* ↥B :=
    { toFun := fun g => ⟨g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹, hxc g⟩
      map_one' := Subtype.ext (by simp)
      map_mul' := fun g h => Subtype.ext (hkey g h) }
  have hker : φ.ker = A := by
    refine le_antisymm (fun g hg => ?_) (fun a ha => ?_)
    · have hgx : g * x = x * g := by
        have hg1 : g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ = 1 := congrArg Subtype.val hg
        have h2 : g * x * g⁻¹ * x⁻¹ * x * g = x * g := by rw [hg1]; group
        rw [← h2]
        group
      rw [← hcent]
      refine Subgroup.le_centralizer_iff.mp ?_ (Subgroup.mem_zpowers g)
      rw [← hDeq]
      refine sup_le (le_trans hBcen (Subgroup.center_le_centralizer _)) ?_
      refine Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr fun w hw => ?_
      obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := hw
      exact Commute.zpow_left (show Commute g x from hgx) n
    · have hax : a * x = x * a := congrArg Subtype.val (hab ⟨a, ha⟩ ⟨x, hxA⟩)
      have hker1 : φ a = 1 := Subtype.ext (by
        show a * x * a⁻¹ * x⁻¹ = 1
        rw [hax]
        group)
      exact hker1
  have hindex : A.index = p ^ 2 := by
    have hmul := A.card_mul_index
    rw [hA2, hcard, show (p : ℕ) ^ 4 = p ^ 2 * p ^ 2 by ring] at hmul
    exact Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_left (pow_pos hp.pos 2) hmul
  have hle : A.index ≤ p := by
    rw [← hker, Subgroup.index_ker, ← hBcard]
    exact Nat.le_of_dvd Nat.card_pos (Subgroup.card_subgroup_dvd_card _)
  rw [hindex] at hle
  have hp2 := hp.two_le
  nlinarith [hle, hp2]

/-- **A group of order `p ^ 4` has an abelian normal subgroup of index `1` or `p`.**  Take an
abelian normal subgroup `A` that is maximal among such subgroups; it is its own centralizer, so
its order is a power `p ^ m` with `m ≤ 4`.  If `A` were central then it would coincide with its
centralizer, the whole group, forcing `m = 4`; this rules out `m = 0`, where `A` is trivial, and
`m = 1`, where `A` is generated by any of its nontrivial elements and one of these is central.
The case `m = 2` is excluded by the commutator homomorphism into the centre.  So `m` is `3` or
`4`, and the index of `A` is `p` or `1` accordingly. -/
theorem exists_abelian_normal_index_le {G : Type*} [Group G] [Finite G] {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)
    (hcard : Nat.card G = p ^ 4) :
    ∃ A : Subgroup G, A.Normal ∧ (∀ u v : ↥A, u * v = v * u) ∧ (A.index = 1 ∨ A.index = p) := by
  haveI : Fact p.Prime := ⟨hp⟩
  have hG : IsPGroup p G := IsPGroup.of_card hcard
  obtain ⟨A, hAn, hAc, hAmax⟩ := exists_maximal_abelian_normal (G := G)
  haveI := hAn
  have hcent := centralizer_eq_of_maximal_abelian_normal hp hG A hAc hAmax
  refine ⟨A, hAn, hAc, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hmA⟩ := (Nat.dvd_prime_pow hp).mp (hcard ▸ Subgroup.card_subgroup_dvd_card A)
  have hcen4 : A ≤ Subgroup.center G → m = 4 := by
    intro hsub
    have htop : A = ⊤ := by
      rw [← hcent, Subgroup.centralizer_eq_top_iff_subset]
      exact hsub
    have hpow : p ^ m = p ^ 4 := by rw [← hmA, htop, Subgroup.card_top, hcard]
    exact Nat.pow_right_injective hp.two_le hpow
  have hmul := A.card_mul_index
  rw [hmA, hcard] at hmul
  interval_cases m
  · refine absurd (hcen4 ?_) (by norm_num)
    rw [Subgroup.eq_bot_of_card_eq A (by simpa using hmA)]
    exact bot_le
  · refine absurd (hcen4 ?_) (by norm_num)
    rw [pow_one] at hmA
    have hAbot : A ≠ ⊥ := fun h => by
      rw [h, Subgroup.card_bot] at hmA
      exact hp.one_lt.ne hmA
    obtain ⟨z, hzA, hzcen, hz1⟩ := exists_mem_center_of_ne_bot hp hG A hAbot
    have hzle : Subgroup.zpowers z ≤ A := Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hzA
    have hzcard : Nat.card ↥(Subgroup.zpowers z) = p := by
      rcases hp.eq_one_or_self_of_dvd _ (hmA ▸ Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le hzle) with h | h
      · exfalso
        have hzmem : z ∈ (⊥ : Subgroup G) := Subgroup.card_eq_one.mp h ▸ Subgroup.mem_zpowers z
        exact hz1 (by simpa using hzmem)
      · exact h
    rw [← Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hzle (by rw [hmA, hzcard])]
    exact Subgroup.zpowers_le.mpr hzcen
  · exact absurd hmA (card_ne_prime_sq_of_centralizer_eq hp hcard A hAc hcent)
  · right
    rw [show (p : ℕ) ^ 4 = p ^ 3 * p by ring] at hmul
    exact Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_left (pow_pos hp.pos 3) hmul
  · left
    have hone : p ^ 4 * A.index = p ^ 4 * 1 := by rw [mul_one]; exact hmul
    exact Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_left (pow_pos hp.pos 4) hone

end Semiabelian

namespace IsSemiabelian

/-- **Every group of order `p ^ 4` is semiabelian.**  Burnside's counting argument supplies an
abelian normal subgroup of index `1` or `p`.  In the first case the group itself is abelian; in
the second the index is the smallest prime factor of `p ^ 4`, so the covering criterion for an
abelian subgroup of least prime index applies. -/
theorem of_card_eq_prime_pow_four {G : Type} [Group G] [Finite G] {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)
    (h : Nat.card G = p ^ 4) : IsSemiabelian G := by
  obtain ⟨A, -, hAc, hidx⟩ := Semiabelian.exists_abelian_normal_index_le hp h
  rcases hidx with h1 | hpi
  · have htop : A = ⊤ := Subgroup.index_eq_one.mp h1
    refine of_mul_comm fun u v => ?_
    have huv := hAc ⟨u, by rw [htop]; trivial⟩ ⟨v, by rw [htop]; trivial⟩
    simpa using congrArg Subtype.val huv
  · exact of_abelian_of_index_eq_minFac A hAc (by rw [hpi, h, hp.pow_minFac (by norm_num)])

end IsSemiabelian
